    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **52 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp38Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain email blocklist so owner creation is rejected with **400 Bad Request** when the email domain is on the blocklist.\n\nChanges, following the codebase's existing per-rule exception convention (mirroring `InvalidEmailException`):\n\n1. **`DisposableEmailDomainException`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending domain.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1`** \u2014 added a `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` set (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) and extended `normalizeEmail(...)` to extract the domain (after the existing syntactic validation and lower-casing) and throw the new exception on a match. Because the check lives in `normalizeEmail`, it applies to both create (`addOwner`) and `updateOwner`, and matching is case-insensitive since the value is already lower-cased.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` that maps `DisposableEmailDomainException` to a 400 `ProblemDetail` with `errors: [\"email\"]`, consistent with the other email/validation handlers.\n\nA `null` email remains accepted (field is optional), and syntactically valid non-blocklisted domains are unaffected.",
